title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tiddlers/sigil-stage
tags: $:/tags/Global lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/SharktoothSigil
lar-kind: mask-summon
lar-pono-uri: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/masks
lar-alias-for: stage
lar-pattern: <<~\s*stage\s+"?(\d+)"?(?:\s+"?((?:[^"]|"(?!\s*>>))*)"?)?\s*>>
lar-example: <<~ stage "20" "Mischief-Muse">>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<!-- stage — a MASK and the theatrical depth it stands at. THE DEPTH FIRST, THE MASK SECOND: a summon
     answers "how near" before "who".

         <<~ stage "20" "Mischief-Muse">>

     The depth reads on the 0-20 scale the boot seed declares by name, so this sigil carries no band
     table of its own — one scale, one place that writes it:

         <<scale stage "green-room@1..4 -> offstage@5..8 -> upstage@9..12 -> center-stage@13..16
                        -> downstage@17..20">>

     Stage WEIGHTS natural surfacing and never gates; the fourth wall opens at 18 and above.

     A CARRIER'S OWN `~Stage` NAMES SOMETHING ELSE — a lifecycle phase, declared locally by the
     carrier that uses it, one capital apart and owned by that scope. This summon never reaches it. -->

\procedure ~stage(p1:"" p2:"")
<span class="lar-stage"><<p2>> @<<p1>></span>
\end
